From 599d52fd781447ac03ef7a071fd809f89998e472 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 09:02:15 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08111/11362] [outer-loop] ARC re-ask gate: verification pass
 finds the shipped gate was never the one measured

Independent recompute of both overnight runs from their RAW per-cell files and
from the founding measurement's raw attempt records, rather than from the
summaries that reported them. Every headline number reproduced exactly; four
defects and one refuted correction came out of it.

REPRODUCED EXACTLY (160 per-cell JSONs + scored.json):
  net 38 / 38 / 38 across a_off, b_shipped, c_owns; A/A floor 35.
  0 engine-defect re-asks in 160 cells, and 0 in the 9 counterfactual cells.
  reask_budget_seen 0/1/1/0 -- the arms genuinely differed.
  0 server failures, 0 driver exceptions; all 4 hard failures are real content
  failures. Prereg predates the first cell by ~3 min and its sha256 matches.

THE FINDING THAT MATTERS (C4). The founding harness
(arc_induce_confirm_20260731/harness/confirm_ab.py:405-433) issues the re-ask
as an EXTRA /completion call. There is no retry ladder for it to borrow from --
that is CARNOT_ARC_INDUCE_DEFECT_OWNS_ATTEMPTS=1 semantics, which is DEFAULT
OFF. What shipped into generate() CONSUMES an attempt instead. So the shipped
configuration has never been measured, and arm C is not a speculative fix
awaiting evidence: it is the configuration the existing evidence was collected
under. The gate half of that headline was never significant either -- the
identified within-arm contrast (final vs round0) is 2 better / 0 worse on 2
discordant attempts, p=0.5, where p<=0.05 is arithmetically unreachable.

ALSO APPLIED: hard-failure denominator corrected (1-in-160 mixed one arm's
numerator with four arms' denominator; it is 4/160 overall, 1/40 for
b_shipped); exposure comparator corrected to the gate's 25% FIRE rate rather
than the 61% control defect rate; the pro-gate alternative reading (3/78
defective gate-OFF vs 0/78 gate-ON) named and rebutted mechanically at the
single counter increment site; scorer wording reconciled; A/A floor's
seed-base-with-position confound declared.

REFUTED, and recorded as such: the proposed replacement figure "23/36 = 64%"
appears nowhere in the corpus. confirm_scored.json carries
control_accepted_a_defective_candidate 22 of 36, recomputed independently as
22 (61.1%). 22/36 is BOTH the treatment usable count and the control
defective-accept count -- a genuine coincidence that misled the review.

TWO GUARD DEFECTS FIXED:
  * _fisher_exact_2x2 used an ABSOLUTE tie-breaking epsilon (v <= obs + 1e-12).
    On the near-perfectly-separated 23/23 vs 0/93 table obs is 8.8e-25, far
    below the epsilon, so the tail summed every table under 1e-12. Reported
    2.3e-14 where the truth is 8.81e-25. Direction was conservative, so no
    conclusion moves. The contingency table was re-derived from the 116 corpus
    files and reproduces exactly.
  * prove_inertness.py reported a VACUOUS pass once its subject was committed:
    the baseline is `git show HEAD:<target>`, so after the commit the diff is
    empty and checks 1-3 pass by having nothing to examine -- while
    overwriting inertness_proof.json with an empty report. A check with no
    subject abstains; it must never render as a pass. Adds Check 0 (fails
    closed, refuses to overwrite the proof, names the pre-change commit for
    --baseline) and records baseline_ref in the proof so it is reproducible.
    Verified both paths: exit 1 on the vacuous case, exit 0 and byte-identical
    evidence on --baseline e5c5a976e.

No shipped default changed. Both goal/engine defect flags remain OFF.
No scored or online ARC game was played.

